# Paul Trap Analysis Toolkit

## Project Overview
This project is a toolkit for developing and analyzing RF Paul traps. It provides functionality to analyze electric properties, trapping parameters, and multipole control of trap designs.

## Main Components
- [PaulTrapAnalysis/components/Electrode.py](mdc:PaulTrapAnalysis/components/Electrode.py): Defines the Electrode class for representing electrode potentials with 3D grid points.
- [PaulTrapAnalysis/components/Trap.py](mdc:PaulTrapAnalysis/components/Trap.py): The Trap class combines electrodes and trap parameters.
- [PaulTrapAnalysis/components/Multipoles.py](mdc:PaulTrapAnalysis/components/Multipoles.py): Handles multipole expansion of trapping potentials.
- [PaulTrapAnalysis/components/Particle.py](mdc:PaulTrapAnalysis/components/Particle.py): Represents trapped particles.
- [PaulTrapAnalysis/components/Trajectory.py](mdc:PaulTrapAnalysis/components/Trajectory.py): Analyzes particle trajectories.

## Function Modules
- [PaulTrapAnalysis/functions/potentials.py](mdc:PaulTrapAnalysis/functions/potentials.py): Functions for handling electric potentials.
- [PaulTrapAnalysis/functions/spherical_harmonics.py](mdc:PaulTrapAnalysis/functions/spherical_harmonics.py): Spherical harmonics calculations.
- [PaulTrapAnalysis/functions/gradients.py](mdc:PaulTrapAnalysis/functions/gradients.py): Gradient calculations for potentials.
- [PaulTrapAnalysis/functions/plotting.py](mdc:PaulTrapAnalysis/functions/plotting.py): Visualization utilities.
- [PaulTrapAnalysis/functions/utils.py](mdc:PaulTrapAnalysis/functions/utils.py): General utility functions.

## Examples
- [notebooks/example.ipynb](mdc:notebooks/example.ipynb): General examples of using the toolkit.
- [notebooks/Etrap-analysis.ipynb](mdc:notebooks/Etrap-analysis.ipynb): Analysis of E-traps.
- [notebooks/Etrap-BEM.ipynb](mdc:notebooks/Etrap-BEM.ipynb): Boundary Element Method analysis.
